@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-use-strict-rfc-6902-patch-semantics
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use strict RFC 6902 patch semantics"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need standard JSON Patch support for persisted and exchanged JSON documents. The API must
+avoid aliasing or mutating its caller's document.
+
+## Decision
+
+Implement the six operations in RFC 6902 and RFC 6901 pointer semantics, validating operation shape
+and target paths strictly. Work on a JSON-compatible deep copy and deep-copy inserted or compared
+values so the result is detached from both the input document and patch values.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Invalid operations and failed path, test, or move conditions throw. Array insertion, root replacement,
+escaped pointer tokens, and structural JSON equality are covered by deterministic tests.
